        "summary": "Solid 3 emits intense red Eu(III) luminescence under 313 nm excitation; lines sharpen at 77 K and intensity roughly halves from 77 K to 300 K. The 5D0→7FJ (J=0–4) pattern, including a 5D0→7F0 line and splitting of 7F1–4, indicates a low-symmetry Eu3+ site. Emission is stronger than EuCl3 and mononuclear Eu–CB[6] under the same conditions.",
